          "email": "timday@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-23 02:22:42.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-18687 llite: check mmap_lock with mmap_assert_locked()",
        "message": "LU-18687 llite: check mmap_lock with mmap_assert_locked()\n\nour_vma() asserts that the caller holds mmap_lock by expecting\nmmap_write_trylock() to fail.  The kernel removed that function in\nv6.5-rc4-110-gcf95e337cb63, so it is only available through a\nlustre_compat replacement.\n\nUse mmap_assert_locked() instead, which checks the lock on kernels\nbuilt with lockdep or CONFIG_DEBUG_VM, and backfill it for kernels\nthat still have mmap_sem.  Remove the mmap_write_trylock() replacement\nand its configure check.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ib7a337fcb69dec87ea9d40e2524f2c206a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
